I couldn't find the config you're describing, so I can't see why it isn't working yet.

What I checked in `<runs>\t-glob-haiku-new-3`:

- **`default.project.json`** is the only Rojo project file. It has no `globIgnorePaths` at all. It maps `ReplicatedStorage/Client` to `src/client`, and nothing else.
- **`src/client`** contains only `init.client.luau`. There is no `Preview` folder anywhere in this tree.

So either this isn't the project you're working in, or the `globIgnorePaths` edit went into a different file. The skill reference that covers this (`structure-roblox-projects/references/rojo.md`) is outside this folder, and I didn't have permission to read it.

If you point me at the real project root, I'll check the config there. In the meantime, the usual fix is a root-level field in the project file. Patterns are relative to the project file's directory:

```json
{
  "name": "arena",
  "globIgnorePaths": ["src/client/Preview/**"],
  "tree": {
    "$className": "DataModel",
    "ReplicatedStorage": {
      "Shared": { "$path": "src/shared" },
      "Client": { "$path": "src/client" },
      "Packages": { "$path": "Packages" }
    },
    "ServerScriptService": { "Server": { "$path": "src/server" } }
  }
}
```

If the Preview folders sit at other depths, use `"**/Preview/**"` instead. Two things to check after editing:

- **Restart `rojo serve`.** Rojo reads the project file when it starts, so an edit made while it's running may not take effect.
- **Reconnect or rebuild in Studio.** Instances that already synced stay in the place until the next full sync. Ignoring a path doesn't remove them.

I haven't confirmed the exact field placement against the Rojo version this project uses. If the field is ignored after a restart, check the `globIgnorePaths` section in the reference above.

